 ## Overview
-This family of methods refines the geometric properties of a mesh $M$ generated by Marching Cubes by adjusting vertex positions to minimize the distance to the true isosurface $f(\mathbf{x}) = I$ or to improve mesh quality metrics such as aspect ratio [Vertex Position Optimization and Error Minimization](10991-vertex-position-optimization-and-error-minimization.md). It sets itself apart from sibling methods by focusing on continuous geometric optimization rather than topological simplification [Mesh Simplification and Optimization](8588-mesh-simplification-and-optimization.md) or boundary closure [Marching Cubes Boundary Cap](13166-marching-cubes-boundary-cap.md).
+This family of methods modifies the geometric properties (vertex positions) of a mesh generated by Marching Cubes to minimize the distance to the true isosurface or improve mesh quality metrics, while keeping the topology fixed by the parent algorithm's lookup tables. It sets itself apart from [Mesh Simplification and Optimization](8588-mesh-simplification-and-optimization.md) by preserving triangle count and connectivity, and from [Marching Cubes Boundary Cap](13166-marching-cubes-boundary-cap.md) by focusing on surface fidelity rather than boundary closure.
 
